# E2: the eight-seat quad arm c2-packed-tp4-8-best-quad (E1 plus QWEN_FAST_QUAD_DRAFT_BLOCKS=2: one 64-row quad draft per block of four seats, (0,1,2,3) and (4,5,6,7)). Its control is E1.
# FIRST HARDWARE RUN of the second quad: the trace for slots 4-7 and the DRAM headroom for two quads (estimated, not measured) are unproven.
# READ: c2_smoke_check clean under its block rules: judged on concurrent8_steady, EXACTLY TWO engaged markers (slots 0,1,2,3 and slots 4,5,6,7), at least one [PACKED-SELECT] round naming both groups
# with users=8, no fallback line and no disable line. concurrent8_code_equal texts equal to E1's and to solo. A capture refusal falls back to pairs and logs a fallback, which the smoke counts
# as a failure: record which quad and the headroom figures. The smoke here adds concurrent8_steady so the rules apply. Duration (estimate): 120 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8-best-quad
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent8_code,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_steady,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
